<div class="card readme-card">
  <h3>Registry Workflow</h3>
  <p class="readme-intro">Registration, approval, execution, effectiveness assessment, and follow-up decisions are separate stages. Use the appropriate workspace for each action.</p>
  <div class="readme-table-wrap"><table class="readme-table"><thead><tr><th>Workspace / control</th><th>Purpose and behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Executive Dashboard</td><td>Portfolio overview, site snapshot, top exceptions, action table, and narrative. Filters also scope the approval queue and Gantt. Screenshot Mode shows the existing executive snapshot, all filtered action rows, and narrative.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Submission &amp; Updates</td><td>Register a new action, inspect an existing plan, update execution, upload evidence, and view update history.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Approvals &amp; Feedback</td><td>Review pending proposals, approve/return/decline the current plan version, inspect review history, and add leadership feedback. The badge counts pending plans within the current filters, not just plans you can approve.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Register New Action Plan</td><td>Explicitly starts a blank registration. After successful registration or existing-plan selection, the registration fields stay greyed out. Registration requires a verified, active user with Can_Submit checked.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Approve Plan</td><td>Sets the reviewed plan to Ongoing automatically and allows execution. The reviewer must be active, have Can_Approve checked, and have the plan's site or department listed in Approval_Sites. Scopes come from Settings (Site or Site/Department). Global is a literal scope, not permission for every site or department. Approval does not prove execution or effectiveness.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Effectiveness &amp; Decisions</td><td>Assess Ongoing, On Hold, or Completed actions using an active account with Can_Audit checked. Approval-enrolled plans need current-version approval. Record impact, behavior changes, observation dates, attribution, evidence, effectiveness rating, and a follow-up decision with an active owner and review date. Each save appends Assessment_Log and updates the master assessment pointer; earlier assessments remain available. Recorded KPI snapshots are latest values at assessment time, not period-specific aggregates.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Assessment defaults</td><td>Owner and expected KPI objective reuse the current plan. The first observation start is suggested from the planned start, explicitly labeled for confirmation; subsequent assessments suggest the day after the previous current-plan observation end. End defaults to today in Manila. Dates remain editable to match evidence, including overlapping periods; future observation dates are blocked. Approval and upload dates are not actual execution or observation dates. Ratings, observed impact and causal explanations remain human judgments.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Google Chat delivery</td><td>Configure the private webhook before enabling delivery. Active Can_Admin maintainers can pause/resume and send assignment notices or eligible due reminders. Notices are consolidated in the shared Chat space, naming owners and escalation contacts. No direct messages or emails are sent. Manual sending does not install the daily trigger; its maintainer installs it in Apps Script.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Verified follow-through</td><td>Each new assessment creates an Open delivery commitment and a separate next effectiveness review commitment. Continue with identical completion and review dates uses one combined review commitment. Each commitment records a deliverable, active owner, independent Can_Audit verifier, completion deadline and a separate effectiveness review date. Owner records progress or blockage, then submits evidence. The verifier closes, returns, or explicitly withdraws it with a reason. Completing a commitment does not prove effectiveness or approve scaling. Earlier plan commitments remain open until explicitly resolved.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Overdue and three strikes</td><td>Deadline dates run through end of day in Asia/Manila. Unresolved commitments are overdue the next day. A confirmed notification suppresses further notices for that commitment and owner/verifier phase for 24 hours. Confirmed overdue messages earn strikes 1, 2 and 3; second and third reminders name mapped manager and executive contacts in the same Chat space. Strikes cap at three. While awaiting verification, the verifier has a separate deadline (default two calendar days) and escalation count. Notes do not reset strikes; approved extensions preserve the original deadline and history. Weekends are included.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Plan change notices</td><td>Successful registrations, revisions, reviews, execution updates, feedback, assessments and follow-up changes append a notice to Registry_Chat_Outbox. Only new changes are queued; historical records are not replayed. Maintainers may preview or send Plan Updates. The separate 15-minute Apps Script trigger delivers queued notices and new assignment messages; the daily trigger handles due reminders. The webhook stays in Script Properties. Pause applies to all Chat delivery. Notification failures do not reverse saved changes. Each queued event is deduplicated; unknown send outcomes require reconciliation before retry.</td></tr><tr><td class="readme-term">Chat operation</td><td>Assessors and maintainers may preview content and routing exceptions without sending. Only Can_Admin maintainers manage sending, triggers and uncertain outcomes. Notifications are logged before sending; confirmed Chat acceptance earns strikes. Unknown transport or server outcomes remain SENDING until reconciled, preventing blind retries. An accepted message is not proof of reading. Content is summarized to fit bounded shared-space messages; up to 100 eligible commitments are processed per run.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Executive impact reporting</td><td>Effectiveness counts and the Impact narrative follow all dashboard filters. All plans in scope are counted, including Completed and Cancelled. Assessed includes Insufficient Evidence; missing ratings are Not Yet Assessed. Unknown ratings are shown separately and excluded from assessed totals. Completion and goal attainment do not automatically validate impact.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Review accountability</td><td>Current-version review status is grouped by site and department. Eligible reviewers have Active, Can_Approve and matching Approval_Sites; this does not assign a single accountable reviewer. Days waiting use the current plan-version submission date in Manila calendar days, not original creation for revised plans. Missing dates are not estimated. Reviewer activity counts the latest recorded decision per current plan, not a performance score or SLA.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Effectiveness ratings</td><td>Validated: clear evidence of desired impact, expectations Met, and a Supported relationship. Partially Effective: some impact, but insufficient or inconsistent. No Observable Effect: Completed action with expectations Not Met and supporting evidence. Insufficient Evidence: too early or too little evidence to assess impact. File presence alone does not select a rating.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Next decision</td><td>Continue, Adjust, Stop, or Recommend Scaling. Every decision records rationale, active accountable owner, and a next effectiveness review date plus a specific completion commitment. Stop does not automatically cancel execution; Adjust does not revise the approved plan. Use the existing owner workflows when a plan or execution change is needed.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Recommend Scaling</td><td>Requires Validated impact, Sustained results, repeatability evidence, transferability/adaptations, and an Acceptable risk review with explanation. This is a recommendation for the governing team, not rollout authorization. The Scaling category alone does not grant approval to scale.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Return / Decline</td><td>A reason is required. A returned proposal must be revised and resubmitted by its owner. Declining a proposal cancels it.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Update Execution</td><td>For the permitted action owner: records current performance, execution status, and an update comment. Submit Update retains approval and does not create a new plan version.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Revise Plan</td><td>Changes the proposal and creates a new plan version requiring approval. It resets execution to Not Started and preserves historical reviews and evidence. Cancel Editing exits the revision form.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Leadership Feedback</td><td>Requires Can_Comment. Feedback is independent of approval, execution, and effectiveness; posting a comment does not approve a plan.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Execution Evidence</td><td>Only the active owner may upload when execution is permitted and uploads are configured. Completion requires a current-plan-version file that is still available in the configured folder. A file's presence does not establish adequacy or effectiveness. Maximum 10 MB per file.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Time-phased Glide Path</td><td>Choose Yes or No. Yes requires an HTTPS Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, or Slides link containing dated milestones or KPI targets. Ensure approvers have source access. The app records availability and the link; it does not read the source or calculate actual versus glide path. Source edits are external to plan versioning; changes to approved milestones should be submitted as a proposal revision.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="readme-term">Governance outcome</td><td>Available for Standardization / Governance Projects. Requires current problem, expected outcome, acceptance criteria and verification method instead of numeric KPI values. Owners record progress in update comments and upload execution proof. Assessors explain evidence against each criterion using the same effectiveness ratings. Completion is delivery; Validated is demonstrated impact. Revisions preserve earlier criteria and require new approval. Blank historical measurement methods retain Numeric KPI behavior.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Account Stability</td><td>Uses current-version approval verified against Review_Log. Counts Ongoing/On Hold and recently Completed plans; excludes pending proposals, cancelled plans and legacy plans without recorded approval. Engagement is reported separately. Duplicate/missing IDs or unknown eligible categories withhold the state. Locked-In needs configured recent Validated and Sustained evidence coverage. Default rules are Proposed, not sponsor-approved. The score is Standardization/Scaling share × 100, not proof of KPI health. Every dashboard filter applies to counts; category/status filters withhold the framework state and show Filtered Mix Only. A narrowed scope is labeled. Completed and evidence windows use Manila calendar days. Ties show Mixed / Review Needed. Maintainers edit Stability_Rules and reload; changing a rule does not rewrite history.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Engagement</td><td>Active Action_Framework rows are supported, including Incentivized Activity and Non - Incentivized Activity. These support morale and participation; they are complementary to the primary KPI intervention. Evidence and outcome measurement are still required before claiming effectiveness.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Executive Capture</td><td>Screenshot Mode shows the current portfolio snapshot, action table and executive narrative. Operational notices and loading overlays are hidden. The exit control is below the report; Esc also exits. Print from Screenshot Mode to omit the exit toolbar. The As of date describes current data: this is not a saved historical month-end or week-end snapshot. Weekly narrative activity refers to the current Sunday–Saturday week; it must not be presented as a completed-week or monthly activity total.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Scope</td><td>Channel, LOB, and Cohort use the Settings lists. A Targeted cohort requires Cohort Details. Approval sites are assigned independently in Access_Control.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">KPI inputs</td><td>Percentages: 82% or 0.82. AHT: HH:MM:SS or decimal minutes. Count: non-negative whole numbers. Other numeric KPIs use their configured units and direction.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Existing records</td><td>Historical Action IDs remain unchanged, including MYQ IDs; their site is displayed as MTQ. Existing plans without Approval_Required enabled retain the legacy execution path.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="readme-term">Loading and saving</td><td>A moving bar indicates work in progress; it is not a measured percentage. Buttons show saving state and prevent repeated submissions. Failed requests display an error. Retry unchanged fields as instructed; success is shown only after the server confirms the operation.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
</div>

