            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td class="readme-term">Days Left</td>
              <td>Calendar days remaining until the Target End Date. 0 displays as Due Today. A negative number means the action is past due. Completed or Cancelled actions display —.</td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td class="readme-term">Action Owner</td>
              <td>The accountable owner: an active, listed work account. Only the verified owner may update execution and upload evidence; submission and comment flags are independent.</td>
            </tr>

            <tr><td class="readme-term">Activity / Action Steps</td><td>Activity is the free-text execution method. Action Steps describe specifically how that method will be performed. Several activities in text still represent one plan and one Action ID.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="readme-term">Leadership Feedback</td><td>Independent, timestamped comments by active users with Can_Comment checked. They do not modify execution, KPI results, review, or effectiveness.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="readme-term">Execution Evidence</td><td>Completed plans have read-only execution, plan details and execution evidence; saved history remains visible and separate effectiveness assessments remain available. Upload a supporting file before completion. Not Started plans may add proof later. New transitions to Completed require an available artifact for the current plan version; historical Completed records are retained. File presence is not validation of impact.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="readme-term">Review / Effectiveness</td><td>Separate from execution and KPI outcome. New plans are Pending Review and Not Yet Assessed. Unrecorded legacy reviews display Not Recorded. Approvers need an active account, Can_Approve checked, and the action site in Approval_Sites. New plans await approval before execution. Active users with Can_Audit may assess approved Ongoing, On Hold, and Completed plans in Effectiveness &amp; Decisions. Assessment ratings do not change execution automatically.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="readme-term">Scope and reporting limits</td><td>Existing site, owner, KPI, category and status filters apply to the snapshot, all action rows, and executive narrative. Department filtering, category mix, effectiveness counts and first-assessment queue follow the same scope. Category mix describes recorded plans. Account Stability separately evaluates approved active and recently completed core plans using its visible rules and recent evidence coverage. Long screenshots require a full-page capture or clearly labeled continuation pages.</td></tr>

